.TH VAULT-MIRROR 1 "October 2026" "vault" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vault-mirror \- mirror a website into an encrypted vault
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vault mirror
.RB [ \-\-key
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-vault
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-max\-pages
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-max\-bytes
.IR SIZE ]
.RB [ \-\-timeout
.IR DURATION ]
.I URL
.RI [ FOLDER ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vault mirror
crawls the website at
.I URL
and stores every page and asset it finds in the vault, beneath
.IR FOLDER / HOST
(or just
.I HOST
if no folder is given).
.PP
The crawl is single threaded: one request at a time, in breadth-first order.
It follows only links on the same host (and port) as
.IR URL ,
and only redirects to that host; a redirect elsewhere skips the page.
Requests are sent with a Chrome user agent string, and certificates are
always verified.
.PP
Links in HTML start tags
.RB ( href ,
.BR src ,
.BR action
and
.B poster
attributes) and CSS
.RB ( url(...)
in style sheets,
.B <style>
elements and
.B style
attributes) that point into the mirror are rewritten to relative paths, so
the copy browses correctly once fetched out of the vault. Relative links are
resolved against the page's final address and its
.B <base href>
if it has one. Links to other hosts, script and comment text, and every
other byte of the page are left as they were. Fragments are kept.
.PP
Pages are named after their URL path. A path that is empty or ends in
.B /
becomes
.BR index.html ;
a query string is appended as
.BI _ query
(URL-escaped). A name already stored by an earlier run is replaced, but if
two different URLs in one crawl would get the same name, the second is
skipped rather than overwriting the first.
.PP
A page that fails to download, answers with anything but
.BR "200 OK" ,
or exceeds a limit is reported on standard error as
.BI "skipping " URL ": " reason
and skipped; the crawl carries on. HTML and CSS are rewritten in memory;
other files are staged in a private temporary file (plaintext on disk
meanwhile) that is always removed. The vault is locked exclusively for the
whole run.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-pages " N"
Pages and assets to fetch at most. Default 10000.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-bytes " SIZE"
Total bytes to download at most, counted after decompression. Default 4G.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " DURATION"
Deadline for each request. Default 5m.
.TP
.BI \-\-key " PATH"
Key file. Default: $VAULT_KEY, else ~/.vault/key.
.TP
.BI \-\-vault " DIR"
Vault directory. Default: $VAULT_DIR, else ~/.vault/store.
.PP
A single HTML or CSS file larger than 16 MiB is skipped.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when everything found was stored, 3 when some of it was skipped, 1 on
an error that stops the crawl.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VAULT_PASSPHRASE
Passphrase, instead of prompting on the terminal.
.SH EXAMPLES
Mirror a site into the vault under
.BR example.com/ :
.PP
.RS
vault mirror https://example.com/
.RE
.PP
Mirror it under a folder, then fetch the front page:
.PP
.RS
vault mirror https://example.com/ archive/2026
.br
vault get archive/2026/example.com/index.html
.RE
.SH LIMITATIONS
URLs assembled by scripts, and
.B srcset
lists, are neither followed nor rewritten. In attribute values only numeric
character references and
.BR &amp; ,
.BR &lt; ,
.BR &gt; ,
.BR &quot; ,
.B &apos;
and
.B &nbsp;
are decoded. There is no rate limit or robots.txt handling; only mirror
sites you may copy.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vault (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Andy Dixon <vault@dixon.cx>, https://www.dixon.cx
